        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "56aaa165-167d-5970-ba3e-d74da0b0cc47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Newman, Robert Redford, Robert Shaw, Tony Bill, Michael Phillips, Julia Phillips\n- Films: Cars, Cars 3, The Sting\n- Characters: Doc Hudson\n- Companies: Disney-Pixar, Pixar\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Picture\n\nFacts:\n- The Sting is a 1973 American caper film set in September 1936 about two professional grifters, played by Paul Newman and Robert Redford, who try to con a mob boss played by Robert Shaw.\n- Tony Bill produced The Sting and shared the Academy Award for Best Picture for the film with Michael Phillips and Julia Phillips.\n- In the 2006 Pixar film Cars, Doc Hudson is an animated anthropomorphic retired race car who serves as a medical doctor and local judge.\n- Paul Newman voiced Doc Hudson in the first Cars film from Disney-Pixar.\n- Paul Newman received a posthumous credit for his Doc Hudson voice recordings in Cars 3, released in 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
